            ╭ D E T A I L ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
            │  Keep Awake  [built-in]  [macOS and Linux]                                                   │
            │  Keep your computer awake for a set time or until you stop it, on macOS or Linux. By default │
            │  it also nudges the cursor once you go idle, so chat apps don't mark you Away. Start a       │
            │  session, come back later and run Stop. CLI/desktop only.                                    │
            │                                                                                              │
            │  PARAMETERS                                                                                  │
            │                                                                                              │
            │  > Action   < Start a session >                                                              │
            │      Start a new session, stop the running one, or check what's currently active.            │
            │                                                                                              │
            │    Session Length   1 hour                                                                   │
            │      How long to stay awake. Ignored for Stop and Check status.                              │
            │                                                                                              │
            │    Display   Keep display awake (recommended)                                                │
            │      Keep the display awake so it doesn't sleep. Allow sleep if you only need background     │
            │      tasks to keep running. On Linux, GNOME needs gnome-session-inhibit for this.            │
            │                                                                                              │
            │    Activity Simulation   After 2 minutes idle (recommended)                                  │
            │      Keeping the computer awake doesn't reset the idle timer, so chat apps still mark you    │
            │      Away. This nudges the cursor 1px once you've been idle this long. macOS needs           │
            │      Accessibility permission for your terminal app; Linux needs an X11 session with xdotool │
            │      and xprintidle.                                                                         │
            ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
